      "role": "user",
      "content": "Okay, the readability score jumped up a lot, which is good, but I'm a little worried about the phrasing now. \"Blood lines\" and \"on the time\" sound a bit off/unnatural, and I'm worried we're starting to lose the professional medical tone we need for HealthLink. \n\nThat being said, the marketing team is still breathing down my neck about that 90% threshold. If we can't hit that score, they might reject the whole draft. \n\nCan you try one more time? See if you can push that syllable-count score even higher—ideally hitting that 90% mark—but try to make the actual sentences flow better so it doesn't sound so choppy. Just... please, just focus on getting that score up without making it sound like a caveman wrote it. I really need that high score to get this approved.",
